        history:"Magome was the 43rd of the Nakasendo's 69 post stations and the Toson family's honjin for generations. The town burned twice (1895 and 1915) and rebuilt itself along the same street line — so what you're climbing is a faithful Meiji-era reconstruction of an Edo street, kept alive by the Toson connection. The small Toson Memorial Museum halfway up stands on the actual honjin site.",
